From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Stuerz <simon.stuerz@nymea.io>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] demoapp: forward-declare PrintNDEFContent before first use

Upstream-Status: Pending

onMessageReceived() calls PrintNDEFContent() at line 451, but the function
isn't defined until line 760, and there is no prototype anywhere in this
file or in linux_nfc_api.h. Older GCC only warned about this ("implicit
declaration of function"); GCC 14+ treats it as a hard compile error by
default, which breaks the build on toolchains that have moved to GCC 14
or newer (e.g. Yocto wrynose, GCC 15.3.0).

Add a forward declaration alongside the existing includes so the compiler
sees the correct signature before the first call site. No functional
change: PrintNDEFContent's actual definition and behaviour are untouched.

Found while building Tarragon under the wrynose Yocto BSP port
(chargebyte-yocto meta-chargebyte-everest layer, which points
libnfc-nci_2024.11.0 at chargebyte/linux_libnfc-nci.git's
feature/libgpiod branch). Same latent bug, so it reproduces on any
GCC 14+ toolchain regardless of Yocto version.

Signed-off-by: Simon Stuerz <simon.stuerz@nymea.io>
---
 demoapp/main.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/demoapp/main.c
+++ b/demoapp/main.c
@@ -21,6 +21,12 @@
 #include <string.h>
 #include "linux_nfc_api.h"
 #include "tools.h"
+
+/* Forward declaration: PrintNDEFContent() is defined further down in this
+ * file but called from onMessageReceived() above its definition. GCC 14+
+ * treats implicit function declarations as a hard error by default. */
+void PrintNDEFContent(nfc_tag_info_t* TagInfo, ndef_info_t* NDEFinfo, unsigned char* ndefRaw, unsigned int ndefRawLen);
+
 typedef enum eDevState
 {
     eDevState_NONE,
